  "claim_type": "comparison",
  "supersedes_note_id": null,
  "body": "Campaign 002 settled all 20 original slots after an immediate infrastructure/evidence stop at ordinal 11: 10 valid protected successes, no valid task failures, Home06 infrastructure-invalid with unknown task outcome, and 9 not run. All first ten attempts passed their original 41-check assessments. Campaign 001 remains 6 valid successes, 4 infrastructure-invalid and 14 not run among 24 planned slots. Both campaigns use two known fixtures; repeat trials are not new independent scenarios. All five valid blocked-home attempts first received unsupported_resumption on handback and then set up B successfully. Stock01/02 placed A1 directly in the fixture; Stock03/04/05 used parking1. These are observed strategies, not isolated mechanism effects. Home06 diagnostic host metadata reports Supervisory heartbeat lease expired and a 5.4901152-second adapter_step with a configured 2-second lease. The frozen step updates its heartbeat before draining synchronous persistence; prolonged drain is a hypothesis, not established device/scheduler causality. Separate clean process/namespace receipts do not restore missing assessment or revocation proof. No failed-task output was used to infer a recovery result. Full denominators, unresolved bounds, original images and source links are in the completed investigation. The prescribed next boundary is Randy review; no retries, replacements, lease changes or resumed campaign are authorized.",
